# INTRODUCTION

| Phase                          | Year (approx.) | What happens                                                                                                                                                               |
| ------------------------------ | -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **1. Spark**                   | 2303-04        | Klara Anders (Ryujin R-Lab) meets mobility-systems engineer Mikhail Rheinhold on a Gagarin contract; they stay in touch.                                                   |
| **2. Shell company**           | 2304           | United Colonies quietly suggests forming **Anders-Rheinhold Systems (ARS)** as a civilian front to explore advanced mech control.                                          |
| **3. Trio completed**          | 2305           | UC introduces freelance mech-architect **Viktor Petrović** (working around Gagarin) to Anders & Rheinhold; all three sign NDAs and lease the back-lot machine shop.        |
| **4. NIC proof-of-concept**    | 2306-07        | ARS builds the **Neural-Interface Conduit (NIC)** for industrial mech arms; night-shift prototypes run successfully.                                                       |
| **5. Project SPEAR green-lit** | mid-2308       | UC awards black-budget Contract Δ-19: turn NIC into a powered exo-suit (**Project SPEAR**).                                                                                |
| **6. The Forge**               | 2308-2310      | Parts milled at Gagarin, labelled “industrial spares,” shipped weekly to a small orbital station nicknamed **The Forge**; first full SPEAR prototype assembled and tested. |
| **7. Armistice clamp-down**    | mid-2311       | War ends; Armistice bans all mech tech. UC freezes SPEAR and seals The Forge as **Black-Vault BV-17-β** “pending audit.”                                                   |
| **8. Corporate collapse**      | 2312           | ARS funding disappears; books closed; Anders, Rheinhold, Petrović all leave public view (“missing”).                                                                       |
| **9. Bureaucratic limbo**      | 2312-present   | BV-17-β receives only minimal maintenance visits; audit never scheduled.                                                                                                   |
| **10. Present hook**           | 2330           | Encrypted beacon from BV-17-β still active; rumours surface; player may investigate.                                                                                       |
